  "body": "It is currently unclear whether UA provided default UIs for certain elements should check events' defaultPrevented status. \r\n\r\nAlso, at which point should the possible default handling happen. During event dispatch (my guess this might happen in blink if it is using shadow DOM without no special event handling) or after the actual DOM event dispatch (this is happening in most cases in Gecko).\r\n\r\nWe need some more testing, but https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1327097#c8 hints that there is no consistency between browsers and blink and gecko don't have even consistency internally.\r\n\r\nMy gut feeling is that web pages should be able to preventDefault() these events.\r\nstopPropagation() shouldn't affect to default handling, nor should UAs call stopPropagation() internally in such way that it is visible to the page.\r\n\r\n@rniwa @dtapuska @tkent @foolip @mounirlamouri ",
